Subject: driver-video-cirrusfb-fix-ram-address-printk-fix
From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>

join the two printk strings to make it atomic.

Cc: Jiri Slaby <jirislaby@gmail.com>
Cc: Philippe De Muyter <phdm@macqel.be>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
---

 drivers/video/cirrusfb.c |    3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff -puN drivers/video/cirrusfb.c~driver-video-cirrusfb-fix-ram-address-printk-fix drivers/video/cirrusfb.c
--- a/drivers/video/cirrusfb.c~driver-video-cirrusfb-fix-ram-address-printk-fix
+++ a/drivers/video/cirrusfb.c
@@ -2432,9 +2432,8 @@ static int cirrusfb_pci_register(struct 
 	info->screen_size = board_size;
 	cinfo->unmap = cirrusfb_pci_unmap;
 
-	printk(KERN_INFO " RAM (%lu kB) at 0x%lx, ",
+	printk(KERN_INFO "RAM (%lu kB) at 0x%lx, Cirrus Logic chipset on PCI bus\n");
 		info->screen_size >> 10, board_addr);
-	printk(KERN_INFO "Cirrus Logic chipset on PCI bus\n");
 	pci_set_drvdata(pdev, info);
 
 	ret = cirrusfb_register(info);
_

